  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1214 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nSurface high pressure remains over the region Monday and then\nbegins to move off to the east Tuesday. At the same time, a ridge\nof high pressure over the Desert Southwest is progged to expand\neastward across the southern Plains through mid week. This ridge\nbroadens out/flattens for the second half of the week with low\nlevel flow becoming more southerly. Temperatures respond with\nupper 70s/lower 80s for highs through Tuesday, and then begin a\nslow warming trend through late week. Low temperatures through \nTuesday morning look to be in the 50s, and then also begin a\nwarming trend. The coolest morning is currently forecast for\nTuesday with potential of the normal cool valley locations of far\nnorthwest Arkansas briefly touching upper 40s. \n\nLatest model solutions continue to highlight an area of low\npressure lifting northeast through the eastern half of the region\nover the weekend. Details at this time remain uncertain, though\nthe potential for rain showers could return next weekend. This \nwill continue to be monitored through the week as latest data come\nin.",
